===Rejected candidates===
*Eduardo Baptista, NATO Staff Officer, Independent;<ref>[https://24.sapo.pt/atualidade/artigos/eduardo-baptista-e-o-primeiro-nome-do-boletim-de-voto-para-as-presidenciais-mas-nao-vai-a-votos “Eduardo Baptista é o primeiro nome do boletim de voto para as presidenciais. Mas não vai a votos“], Sapo (December 30, 2020).</ref>{{efn|Candidate only delivered 11 signatures, of which only 6 were valid, far short of the required 7,500. However, his name appeared on ballots, as they started being printed before the Court officially verified all candidacies' documents. Votes for Eduardo Baptista were counted as invalid.}}

===Unsuccessful candidates===
*Carla Bastos, [[Socialist Party (Portugal)|Socialist Party]] member, Finances inspector;<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.publico.pt/2020/08/27/politica/noticia/ps-ja-militante-quer-presidente-1929320|title=O PS já tem uma militante que quer ser Presidente|first=Luciano|last=Alvarez|website=PÚBLICO|date=27 August 2020 }}</ref>
*Orlando Cruz, former [[CDS – People's Party|People's Party]] member;<ref name="candidatos">{{cite web |date=September 8, 2020 |title=Presidenciais. De André Ventura a Tino de Rans, já são oito os pré-candidatos a Belém |trans-title=Presidentials. From André Ventura to Tino de Rans, there are already eight pre-candidates for Belém |url=https://observador.pt/2020/09/08/presidenciais-de-andre-ventura-a-tino-de-rans-ja-sao-oito-os-pre-candidatos-a-belem/ |access-date=September 8, 2020 |publisher=Observador |language=pt}}</ref>
*Paulo Alves, [[Together for the People]] party member, former member of the [[Felgueiras]] municipal assembly (2005-2009)<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.dn.pt/poder/presidenciais-tem-mais-um-candidato-e-nao-poupa-criticas-a-marcelo-13004238.html|title=Presidenciais têm mais um candidato. E não poupa críticas a Marcelo - DN|website=www.dn.pt|date=5 November 2020 }}</ref>
*Paulo Patinha Antão, [[unemployed]]<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/politica/1598313/patinha-antao-quer-ser-candidato-a-pr-para-ser-rosto-dos-desempregados|title=Patinha Antão quer ser candidato a PR para ser rosto dos desempregados|date=October 5, 2020|website=Notícias ao Minuto}}</ref>

===Withdrew===
*Bruno Fialho, [[Democratic Republican Party (Portugal)|Democratic Republican Party]] (PDR) leader;<ref>{{cite web |url=https://expresso.pt/politica/2020-12-12-Presidenciais.-Bruno-Fialho-do-PDR-desiste-de-candidatura-a-Belem|title=Presidenciais. Bruno Fialho do PDR desiste de candidatura a Belém |date=12 December 2020 |language=pt |trans-title=Presidentials. Bruno Fialho of PDR gives up his candidacy to Belém|publisher=Público|access-date=12 December 2020}}</ref>
*[[Gonçalo da Câmara Pereira]], [[People's Monarchist Party (Portugal)|People's Monarchist Party]] (PPM) president, [[fado]] singer, [[actor]] and [[Agriculture|rural producer]]<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PwqLYOvZgYc|title=#221 Gonçalo da Câmara Pereira Desiste da Candidatura Presidencial - Eleições Presidenciais 2021 - YouTube|website=www.youtube.com}}</ref>

===Refused===
*[[Adolfo Mesquita Nunes]], former Secretary of State for Tourism (2013–2015) and [[CDS – People's Party|People's Party]] MP (2011–2013).<ref>{{cite web|title=Adolfo Mesquita Nunes afasta candidatura às Presidenciais|url=https://observador.pt/2020/06/06/adolfo-mesquita-nunes-afasta-candidatura-as-presidenciais/|website=www.observador.pt|publisher=Observador|access-date=June 8, 2020|language=pt}}</ref>
*[[António Sampaio da Nóvoa]], former Rector of the [[University of Lisbon]] (2006–2013); presidential candidate in 2016, polled second place with almost 23 percent of the vote;<ref>[https://www.publico.pt/2018/01/24/video/se-ha-uma-coisa-que-aprendi-e-que-nunca-se-deve-dizer-nunca-a-nada-20180124-001551 “Se há uma coisa que aprendi é que nunca se deve dizer nunca a nada”], Público (January 24, 2018).</ref>
*[[Miguel Albuquerque]], [[Presidents of the Regional Government of Madeira|President of the Regional Government of Madeira]] since 2015; former Mayor of [[Funchal]] (1994–2013).<ref>{{cite web|title=Miguel Albuquerque continua a equacionar candidatura a Belém |date=10 September 2020|url=https://www.dnoticias.pt/2020/9/10/73110-miguel-albuquerque-continua-a-equacionar-candidatura-a-belem/|website=www.dnoticiais.pt|publisher=Diário de Notícias da Madeira|access-date=10 September 2020|language=pt}}</ref>

==Campaign==
[[File:Discurso de André Ventura na noite eleitoral de 2021.jpg|thumb|Chega's Ventura's speech during election night of the 2021 presidential election]]

===Issues===
The campaign was severely limited by the [[COVID-19 pandemic in Portugal|COVID-19 pandemic]], with candidates being forced to reduce campaign events to a minimum due to movement limitations imposed by the Government to prevent the spread of the virus. There were mandatory [[Curfew|curfews]] in several [[Municipalities of Portugal|municipalities]] and movement between all municipalities was prohibited during the weekends.<ref>{{cite web |date=10 January 2021|title=Presidenciais. Campanha oficial para as Presidenciais arrancou, mas com poucas iniciativas  |url=https://eco.sapo.pt/2021/01/10/presidenciais-campanha-oficial-arranca-hoje-mas-com-poucas-iniciativas/ |accessdate=31 December 2024|website=ECO |language=pt-PT}}</ref>

At the beginning of the electoral campaign, the president of the French [[National Rally]] party, [[Marine Le Pen]], confirmed that she would go to Lisbon to support [[André Ventura]]'s presidential candidacy.<ref>{{cite web |title=Presidenciais. André Ventura e Marine Le Pen juntos em Lisboa no início da campanha eleitoral |url=https://observador.pt/2020/12/21/presidenciais-ventura-e-le-pen-juntos-em-lisboa-no-inicio-da-campanha-eleitoral/ |website=Observador |language=pt-PT}}</ref>

